\id GEN — synthetic common-errors fixture
\id GEN
\rem This file is deliberately malformed. Each section is annotated with the
\rem lint code it is intended to trigger.

\p Paragraph before any chapter — content-before-first-chapter.

\c 1
\p
\v 1 First verse text.
\v 1 Duplicate verse number — duplicate-verse-number.
\v 2 Inline unknown marker \foozy here — unknown-marker.
\v 3 Stray close \nd*here — stray-close-marker.
\v 4 Excess     whitespace     in     content — excess-whitespace-in-content.
\v 6 Note submarker \fr 6:6 outside any note — note-submarker-outside-note.
\v 7 Unclosed footnote \f + \fr 7:7 \ft body text but no close

\c 6
\s1 A section paragraph
\v 1 Verse inside section heading — verse-in-section-or-other-paragraph.

\c 7
\v 2 Verse outside an explicit paragraph — verse-outside-explicit-paragraph.
